      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Declaring an immediate, definitive denial when an active breach is confirmed puts the company at risk of legal liability for misrepresenting the situation. Even if you have no hard proof yet, issuing a false statement like \"no unauthorized access\" before the full truth is known could be considered foreseeable knowledge in a securities fraud suit. You cannot use this narrative now, as the delay required to investigate likely exceeds both your market hours and deadlines for a truthful defense.",
